{
  "source": "Prompts/why-answers-vary-5.mp4",
  "duration": 200.8990625,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.42,
      "text": "You ask an AI, what should I name my new dog, and it suggests spot."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.22,
      "end": 10.32,
      "text": "You start a brand new chat, ask the exact same question, and this time it suggests max."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.14,
      "end": 14.5,
      "text": "How did the exact same input yield a totally different result?"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.86,
      "end": 18.5,
      "text": "This outlines three variables controlling the output."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.34,
      "end": 23.94,
      "text": "First, the model. The specific system and computing power change the answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.04,
      "end": 29.6,
      "text": "Second, what AI receives. Prompt and context alter starting conditions."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.36,
      "end": 34.94,
      "text": "Third, the AI's choices. Techniques like sampling and temperature."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.48,
      "end": 40.76,
      "text": "Look at this AI mid-sentence, calculating a probability for every token."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.64,
      "end": 46.52,
      "text": "Spot leads at 22%. You might expect the system to pick it every single time,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.02,
      "end": 53.04,
      "text": "but a 22% probability simply means the AI picks it roughly 22 times out of 100 attempts."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.16,
      "end": 58.62,
      "text": "That process of drawing a token based on a set of weighted odds is known as sampling."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.72,
      "end": 65.46,
      "text": "If we run five random picks against these exact same probabilities, the results look like this."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.32,
      "end": 72.3,
      "text": "Max, spot, buddy, rex, and max again. Even with the highest initial odds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.58,
      "end": 78.4,
      "text": "spot was picked only once. The top probability creates a weighted advantage, not a guarantee."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.18,
      "end": 83.2,
      "text": "If we pull another five random picks, the list of names will likely be completely different."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.3,
      "end": 89.04,
      "text": "Why intentionally design a system this way? Why not force the AI to select the most"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.04,
      "end": 94.48,
      "text": "mathematically likely word every time? If the system always defaulted to the top token,"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.9,
      "end": 98.88,
      "text": "the text generation would become highly repetitive and read like a machine,"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.46,
      "end": 103.68,
      "text": "giving lower probability words a mathematical chance to win the draw,"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.92,
      "end": 106.78,
      "text": "injects variety, and creative phrasing into the responses."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.02,
      "end": 110.68,
      "text": "Choosing a different token shapes what comes next."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.18,
      "end": 116.88,
      "text": "A single variation at this step sends the generated answer down a completely divergent path."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.0,
      "end": 121.5,
      "text": "Sampling is the mechanism that selects the token based on the odds."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.8,
      "end": 125.54,
      "text": "Temperature is the tool that adjusts those underlying odds."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.26,
      "end": 130.14,
      "text": "In everyday consumer interfaces like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Claude,"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.62,
      "end": 134.2,
      "text": "this temperature setting operates in the background, managed for you automatically."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.5,
      "end": 140.86,
      "text": "This chart isolates how temperature works. We begin with the starting odds in the center,"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.28,
      "end": 144.7,
      "text": "the baseline probabilities generated from the training data and your prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.6,
      "end": 150.28,
      "text": "Applying a low-temperature setting concentrates the probability around the leading choices."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.54,
      "end": 157.82,
      "text": "Spot's baseline chance of 22% rises sharply to 36%. The math heavily favors the leader."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.78,
      "end": 161.46,
      "text": "A high-temperature setting achieves the reverse effect."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.86,
      "end": 165.88,
      "text": "It spreads the probability more widely across the lower tier options."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.8,
      "end": 172.42,
      "text": "Because the odds are shared across the board, Spot's probability drops from 22% down to 16%."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.5,
      "end": 176.3,
      "text": "Notice that temperature does not introduce new data."
    },
    {
      "start": 176.9,
      "end": 179.84,
      "text": "Both settings are modifying the exact same baseline odds."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.72,
      "end": 184.92,
      "text": "Spot remains the highest individual token across all three scenarios."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.08,
      "end": 188.5,
      "text": "Temperature simply dictates the degree of its dominance."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.15,
      "end": 193.84,
      "text": "AI answers vary because the system processes three overlapping variables."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.7,
      "end": 197.2,
      "text": "Different inputs, different odds, and different choices."
    }
  ],
